Bond-Leads-Equity Signal: Implementation Specification
Oct 28, 2026 · @A K
1. Purpose and scope
The signal detects an issuer-specific abnormal move in a corporate bond spread, decides if the move is information or liquidity, and trades the issuer's equity when the move is information and the stock has not yet moved.
Outputs per issuer and per bar:
• z: the standardized abnormal bond move.
• mu_hat: the expected equity excess return over the target horizon.
• m: the part of mu_hat that the stock has not yet realized.
• A trade instruction: direction, size, horizon, and exit conditions.
• A diagnostic label: information, liquidity, or already priced.
Two use modes:
• Alpha mode: trade the stock to capture m.
• Hedge mode: trade the stock to hedge a bond inventory position against the information component of the move.
Out of scope for v1:
• The equity-leads-bond direction.
• The cash-CDS basis trade.
• A full capital-structure arbitrage model.
Prior on the result: equity leads credit in most names most of the time. The expected effect concentrates in high-yield names, negative shocks, and CDS-confirmed moves. The build must confirm the effect in Module B before any execution work starts.
The left column runs live on every bar. The right band is fitted offline and hands the response model to Module D.
