Conditional model:
1. v1: linear interactions, gamma_h(x) = theta_h' x, with x standardized and the rating bucket as dummies. Fit by pooled panel regression of r~^E on z times x with the Module B clustering.
2. Shrink theta_h toward the bucket means with a hierarchical prior. Buckets with fewer than 200 events inherit the parent bucket.
3. v2: gradient-boosted trees on (z, x) with a monotone constraint on z. Keep v1 as the fallback and compare out of sample.
4. Expected pattern: |gamma_h| is material only for HY, for wider moves, and with CDS confirmation. In IG the structural loading is near zero, so a spread residual implies a large equity move with a larger error. Do not invert the structural model to get the equity move. The regression shrinks the estimate by itself. Use the structural delta only as a prior on the loading.
8. Module D: signal construction
The signal is the part of the expected equity move that the stock has not yet realized, after four gates.
At each bar t for each issuer with an open event (t_0 within the last h* bars):
\hat\mu = \hat\gamma_{h^*}(x_{t_0})\, z_{t_0}, \qquad m_t = \hat\mu - \tilde r^E_{t_0,t}
Gates, all must pass:
1. Confidence gate: tau = mu_hat / SE(mu_hat) with |tau| >= 2. SE comes from the clustered covariance of theta_{h*}. Option: replace the t-ratio with a split conformal interval for r~^E over h*, calibrated on the last 250 days of events, and require the interval to exclude zero.
2. Liquidity gate: Z_{t_0,t} > -0.5. If more than half of the bond shock has reverted, the move was pressure. Set the signal to zero and close any open position.
3. Awareness gate: the equity awareness features at t_0 are below their 80th percentile. If the equity side already moved, there is no lead to trade.
4. Cost gate: |m_t| >= kappa times the round-trip cost estimate for the intended size, with kappa = 2. Cost = equity half-spread plus square-root impact.
Signal value and label:
• S_{i,t} = m_t when all gates pass, else 0.
• Direction: sign(S). A wider spread gives S < 0 and a short stock position. A tighter spread gives S > 0 and a long stock position.
• Label: information when gates 1 to 3 pass; liquidity when gate 2 fails; already priced when gate 3 fails.
• Ranking across issuers: |tau| times |m_t|. Cap the number of open names by the risk limits in Module E.
Output record per bar: issuer, t_0, z, x, mu_hat, SE, m_t, Z, label, S, h*, and the gate that failed.
9. Module E: position size
Alpha mode sizes on the expected move and its variance. Hedge mode sizes on the dollar hedge ratio and the probability that the move is information.
9.1 Alpha mode
w_{i,t} = f \cdot \frac{m_t}{\hat\sigma^2_{E,h^*}}, \qquad f = 0.25
1. sigma_hat_{E,h*} is the EWMA volatility of r~^E over h* bars, 10-day half-life.
2. Cap |w| at the per-name limit (default 1 percent of the book) and the gross limit (default 20 percent of the book across all open names).
3. Child orders at most 5 percent of the expected 30-minute equity volume.
9.2 Hedge mode
Q_{i} = -\,g_i \cdot \hat\beta_{E,i} \cdot \mathrm{MV}_{\mathrm{bond},i}
1. Q_i is the dollar equity position that hedges the bond inventory of issuer i. A long bond position with a wider spread gives a short equity hedge.
2. beta_hat_E: regression of the daily bond excess return on the daily equity return over 120 days. Sum the cross-covariances at lags -2 to +2 to correct the lead-lag bias at short horizons.
3. Shrink: beta_hat_E = lambda beta_emp + (1 - lambda) beta_Merton, with lambda = n / (n + 60) for n days of data. beta_Merton = (1 - N(d1)) / N(d1) in dollar terms, from the issuer's capital structure.
4. g_i in [0, 1] is the hedge fraction. Set g_i to the posterior probability that the event is information, from the Module C model, and 0 when gate 2 or gate 3 of Module D fails. The hedge covers the information component only. A liquidity move in the bond reverts, and a hedge against it adds risk.
5. Rebalance the hedge at each bar while the event is open, with a 10 percent tolerance band on Q to limit turnover.
10. Module F: entry and exit
Enter at the first bar after the signal passes the gates. Exit on the first rule that fires.
Entry:
1. Trade only in equity hours. An event in the pre-open bucket enters in the opening auction, and only when that bucket has a validated gamma_h in Module B.
2. Post passive at the mid for one bar, then cross the spread for the remainder.
3. Do not enter when a scheduled event falls inside the horizon.
