11. Backtest and validation
The backtest answers one question first: does gamma_h(x) exist out of sample in any bucket after costs? Only then does the execution work start.
Protocol:
1. Walk-forward: 12-month estimation window, 3-month test window, 3-month step. Refit Modules A, B, and C at each step.
2. Availability: every input enters at its report time. No bar uses a quote, a print, or a fundamental that was not known at the bar close.
3. Universe: point-in-time membership. Include issuers that later defaulted or delisted.
4. Costs: equity half-spread plus square-root impact at the child-order size. Bond costs do not apply to the stock leg. In hedge mode, score the variance reduction of the hedged bond book instead of P&L.
Report per bucket and per horizon:
• gamma_hat_h and delta_hat_h with clustered confidence intervals.
• Hit rate, mean r~^E at h* per unit of z, and the cumulative response curve over h.
• Net P&L, Sharpe, turnover, and the number of events.
• Capacity: the book size at which impact consumes half of the gross alpha.
Falsification tests, all required before a go decision:
• Placebo: shift every t_0 by a random 1 to 5 days. gamma_h must fall to zero.
• Asymmetry: rho(k) for k > 0 must differ from rho(-k) in the buckets that trade.
• Stability: the sign of gamma_h at h* is the same in at least 4 of 5 test windows per bucket.
• Sensitivity: the result holds for c_z in {2.0, 2.5, 3.0}, K in {3, 6, 12}, and bar length in {1, 5, 15} minutes.
• Multiple tests: many buckets inflate false positives. Control the false discovery rate at 10 percent across buckets and horizons, and require economic size above the cost gate.
• Leakage check: re-run with the k = 0 equity term removed. The effect must grow. If it falls, the sample has a timestamp error.
Go criteria for v1: at least one bucket with gamma_h* t-stat below -3 after the false discovery control, net Sharpe above 1.0 in that bucket, and the placebo at zero.
12. Live operation and monitoring
The live system recomputes z on every bond quote update and the full signal at every bar close. Model parameters refit after the close.
Runtime:
1. Latency budget: z within 1 second of a quote update; the signal record within 5 seconds of the bar close.
2. Two processes: an event detector (Module A on the quote stream) and a signal engine (Modules C to F on the bar clock). The detector writes events to a queue; the engine reads the queue.
3. Nightly: refit Module A per issuer, refresh the factor betas, recompute beta_E, and rebuild the reference data and the event calendar.
4. Weekly: refit Modules B and C and update h* per bucket.
